# Deno Edge Function Conventions

## File Structure
- Each function lives in its own directory under `supabase/functions/`
- Shared code goes in `_shared/` directory
- Each function directory has its own `deno.json` for dependencies

## Imports
- Use JSR imports for Supabase packages: `jsr:@supabase/functions-js`
- Use URL imports for Deno std library
- Shared imports defined in `_shared/deno.json`

## Edge Function Pattern
- Export a default handler using `Deno.serve()`
- Return proper JSON responses with appropriate status codes
- Handle errors gracefully and return meaningful error messages

## Shared Utilities
- `generateFruit.ts` contains fruit generation and communication functions
- `generateApple()` / `generateOrange()` - create new fruit instances
- `communicateAttributes(fruit)` - human-readable description of fruit
- `communicatePreferences(fruit)` - human-readable preference description

## Testing
- Tests use Deno's built-in test runner
- Test files are named `*.test.ts`
- Import assertions from `std/assert`
